`tests/qa/colors_to_rgba_output_determinism_test.py` calls `matplotlib.colors.to_rgba("#9467bd", alpha=0.625)`. In `lib/matplotlib/colors.py`, `to_rgba` first checks the cache under key `(c, alpha)`; on a miss it computes the value with `_to_rgba_no_colorcycle` and then stores that tuple back in the cache. For a six-digit hex string, `_to_rgba_no_colorcycle` deterministically parses each hex pair with `int(..., 16) / 255` and appends the provided alpha, so `"#9467bd"` always becomes the same RGB floats and alpha `0.625`. Because the computation is pure for these inputs and the cache only memoizes that same result, the returned tuple is identical in every independent execution.

